{"parentUuid":"b866443e-744c-4da7-b275-49b841a11dfa","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"adfe1d740cda6c713","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffqLup8JH4T1Eyds8QVe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written 10 new entries for Chapter 7 lead-in and section 7.1, all through the end of 7.1. Lint flags nothing in my files. I edited no existing entries, did not touch `_book.md`, made no vault edits and ran no git commands. The scope file is `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/_scope_supertraining_ch7a.txt`.\n\n**Entries** (in `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/Flint/staging/library/strength-and-conditioning/supertraining--verkhoshansky/`)\n\n| File | Kind | Confidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| `framework--strength-training-aims-and-method-chart-figs-7-1-and-7-2.md` (chapter \"7\") | framework | untested |\n| `framework--maximal-supramaximal-circa-maximal-and-submaximal-methods.md` | framework | contested |\n| `framework--three-bodybuilding-regimes-and-add-on-methods.md` | framework | untested |\n| `framework--set-structures-plateau-step-stripping-and-pyramids.md` | framework | untested |\n| `framework--interval-resistance-training-and-cluster-sets.md` | framework | contested |\n| `framework--hybrid-repetitions-and-hybrid-sets.md` | framework | untested |\n| `framework--contrast-methods-load-release-pneumatics-heavy-light-set.md` | framework | contested |\n| `framework--miscellaneous-bodybuilding-set-variations.md` | framework | untested |\n| `heuristic--progressive-and-random-segmental-training.md` | heuristic | untested |\n| `heuristic--overcoming-sticking-points-repertoire-of-27-strategies.md` | heuristic | untested |\n\nThat is 8 frameworks and 2 heuristics: 3 contested, 7 untested, none supported or proven.\n\n**Rows for `_book.md`**\n- **7 lead-in:** printed 393-394 / PDF 404-405, 1 entry (the Figs 7.1-7.2 framework). It also carries the 7.1 paragraph on choosing hypertrophy or nervous-system work, so the reader doesn't get a near-duplicate.\n- **7.1:** printed 394-403 / PDF 405-414, 9 entries.\n\n**Where I stopped.** 7.1 runs onto the top of PDF 414 / printed 403: sticking-point items 13-28 and \"Concluding Remarks\" are there, and the 7.2 heading starts mid-page. I atomized that top part and nothing from \"7.2 PNF\" down. PDF 414 should not be given entirely to 7.2.\n\n**Not atomized because existing entries already cover it**\n- The sources-of-knowledge list on PDF 404 repeats Chapter 1.\n- Quasi-isometrics and \"superslow\" (PDF 405) are in `framework--precise-muscle-action-terminology` and `heuristic--eccentric-quasi-isometrics-...`.\n- The connective-tissue emphasis and low-intensity cyclical work (PDF 405) belong to the 1.6.2 material.\n- Compensatory acceleration training (CAT, PDF 411) is in `framework--compensatory-acceleration-training`. The only new thing here is the name \"Compensatory Deceleration Training\".\n- Static-dynamic is in the 4.2.6.3 entry; plyometrics and parachute release are in the Chapter 5 entries.\n\n**Dedup:** neither the vault nor staging had a bodybuilding-methods catalogue, cluster sets, rest-pause, hybrids, contrast sets or a sticking-point list. Zatsiorsky's library entries have no section on methods, and Bompa's folder has nothing on sets and reps.\n\n**Reciprocal-link suggestions**\n- The strength-deficit heuristic and `framework--strength-deficit-jump-comparison-estimate` → the Figs 7.1-7.2 chart entry. Chapter 7 restates the deficit rule in the direction of Chapter 1's \"In general\" sentence.\n- `framework--functional-vs-structural-resistance-training` → chart entry.\n- `framework--compensatory-acceleration-training` → sticking-points item 3, plus a note on the Deceleration name.\n- `claim--static-dynamic-combined-isometric-concentric-method`, both 3.4.2 entries (`claim--pap-findings-contested-...`, `framework--post-activation-potentiation-...`) and the parachute heuristic → contrast methods.\n- `framework--shock-methods-to-break-training-stagnation` → sticking-points entry and miscellaneous variations.\n- Setchinov 5.6 → miscellaneous variations.\n- `framework--aerobic-vs-anaerobic-circuit-parameters` and `framework--continuous-interval-and-mixed-circuit-training-classification` → interval/cluster.\n- Circuit-layout variants, DeLorme and both APRE entries → set structures.\n- Table 1.1 (`framework--resistance-training-prescription-by-goal`) → bodybuilding regimes.\n- `claim--exercise-economy-...` (3.4.6) → interval/cluster and hybrid.\n- `claim--joint-angle-specific-...` and `heuristic--train-force-at-the-accentuated-joint-angle` → segmental.\n- The eccentric-damage entry and `framework--three-methods-for-maximum-strength-...` → maximal methods.\n- Zatsiorsky's sticking-points framework → sticking-points entry.\n\n**Contradictions and unclear spots in the source**\n- **Cluster load (contested):** the minimum cluster load is \"one's 5RM\" (PDF 409), but intensive clustering uses \"75-90% of 1RM\" (PDF 410).\n- **Rest between near-maximal singles (contested):** the weightlifting method gives \"1-5 minutes\" (PDF 406), but PDF 409 says weightlifting uses near-maximal singles \"with a few seconds of rest\".\n- **Heavy-light and load-release methods (contested):** the book's own 3.4.2 Western studies (PDF 175, checked on a crop of the page image) found no speed or jump boost after loaded work.\n- **Intensive clustering wording:** \"4-6 sets of only one repetition ... for 4-6 repetitions\" is garbled (PDF 410).\n- **Hybrid notation:** \"80³ over 3+5+2\" is called \"a set of 3 repetitions\" for a 10-rep set (PDF 411).\n- **Sticking-point list:** it is numbered to 28 but has no item 19, so it holds 27 strategies (PDF 414).\n- **Plateau and step examples:** no unit is given (PDF 408).\n- **Eccentrics:** described under Maximal Methods in the text but listed under Supramaximal in Fig 7.2 (PDF 406-407). This is a filing difference, not a contradiction.\n- **Intensive regime:** its 80-90% sits under Submaximal Methods, which the book defines as 60-80% (PDF 407-408).\n- **Citation spelling:** the page prints \"Nelson & Lamber\"; the existing 3.4.2 entry spells it Lambert.\n- **Fig 7.2 connectors:** checked at 300 dpi. Only explosive strength, flexibility and hypertrophy are linked to methods. The maximal, circa-maximal and submaximal categories and the Oxford Method box have no drawn connectors.\n\n**What I opened and what I didn't.** I rendered and opened every page image from PDF 404 to 414, plus a crop of PDF 175. Not checked, and cited only as the book's own cross-references: the Fig 1.9 equations, Figs 1.8, 1.32, 2.8 and 2.9, and Table 3.12's \"over 60kJ\" clean-and-jerk figure. Every quote from `method-baseline.md` carries its line number and tag: lines 30, 41, 61, 76, 103, 104, 107, 109, 119, 142, 180, 182 and 186.\n\n**Lint output:**\n```\nsupertraining--verkhoshansky/_book.md: body em dash lines [12, 132, 133]\nTOTAL ISSUES: 1\n```\nThe one issue is in `_book.md`, not my files. Each of my 10 files has exactly six em dashes, all in the section headers. No wikilink is wrapped across lines, all wikilinks resolve, and none points to a Chapter 6 file."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_read_input_tokens":276411,"output_tokens":2891,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":39},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":396},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2891,"cache_read_input_tokens":276411,"cache_creation_input_tokens":396,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":396,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CffqLisYrJdDQry